  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively identify the relevant FCC/B2 lamellar Al-Co-Cr-Fe-Ni alloy, the beneficial mechanical interaction of alternating soft FCC and hard B2 phases, and the roles of dislocations, stacking faults, twins, and multiple deformation modes in HEA plasticity. They also establish that high pressure, including combined high-pressure/high-temperature exposure, can substantially transform HEA structures, while related processing can refine phase distributions or produce coherent nanoscale features. However, none applies HPHT to the Al0.7CoCrFeNi lamellar alloy or predicts conversion to a hierarchical FCC/B2 pattern with coherent interfaces and preferential FCC-to-B2 dislocation transfer. Thus the literature points in the right direction, but selecting HPHT to engineer that specific interface architecture and mechanism would require a substantial new idea."
